This directory holds captured RediSearch answers for FT.SEARCH behaviors that
valkey-search currently answers *differently*. It is a demonstration of known
divergences, not a passing compatibility suite: every test in
integration/compatibility_divergence_test.py is marked xfail(strict=True), so CI
stays green while a divergence exists and turns red as soon as one is fixed
without its marker being removed.

To regenerate the answer file, cd to integration/ and run:

    pytest compatibility_divergence/generate_divergence.py

Docker is required. Like the generators in integration/compatibility/, this one
spins up redis/redis-stack-server on port 6380 to capture reference answers, and
the docker handling is sometimes flaky -- the container may need to be killed
manually between runs. The pickle records which search module version answered
(e.g. "search 21020"), so the expectations always name the build they came from.

The pickle also stores a SHA256 of generate_divergence.py alone, and the replay
test verifies it on load. That is narrower than integration/compatibility/, whose
hash covers every .py file in the directory: nothing else here feeds the answers,
and each record carries the setup commands that produced it, so there is no
shared dataset module to guard. Set SKIP_DIVERGENCE_HASH_CHECK=1 to bypass the
check while iterating locally.

Why this is separate from integration/compatibility/ rather than a few more
cases in generate.py: that suite's comparator normalizes away exactly the signals
these bugs live in. unpack_result re-sorts *both* engines' rows by the sort field
before comparing, so an ordering divergence disappears; unpack_search_result
drops the sort-key element, so WITHSORTKEYS values are never compared; and its
2-element stride cannot parse a NOCONTENT reply at all. Cases added there would
pass against every divergence captured here, so the replay side compares replies
raw -- element for element, order and arity included.
